    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 614,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Tartu County\nTartu County ( Tartu maakond ) , or Tartumaa ( Kreis Dorpat ) , is one of 15 counties of Estonia . It is located in eastern Estonia bordering P\u00f5lva County , Valga County , Viljandi County and J\u00f5geva County . The area of Tartu County is 2,992.74 km \u00b2 , which covers 6.9 % of the territory of Estonia . In January 2013 Tartu County had a population of 150,139 -- constituting 11.6 % of the total population in Estonia . The city of Tartu is the centre of the county located at a distance of 186 km from Tallinn . Tartu County is divided into 22 local governments -- 3 urban and 19 rural municipalities ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
